# fh102, the pebble-pocket (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle fh102
revision 1
state ready
dialect frosthollow
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_ulric_stonevein
written_by claude
title the pebble-pocket
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=miner temper=short
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk collects_smooth_stones_from_the_riverbanks
likes roast_pork swimming fresh_straw summer_evenings
dislikes drizzle night_noise
fears a_hard_winter_on_the_pass_road losing_someone_to_the_snow
hopes a_sill_full_of_river_stones a_winter_where_nobody_is_lost
topics pastimes +0.4 food +0.3 work +0.3 memories +0.2 weather +0.2 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=plain refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# digs ore up at the mine and fills every pocket with smooth stones off the riverbank: quick to flare and quicker to say sorry, warm underneath, and forever looking down the pass road in winter.

words
oath! = River take it | Pick and pebble | Rough rock, smooth water
saying! = Water's patient, rock never is | Every pebble was a cliff once | Give it a river and time
pebble = a river pebble | a smooth one off the bank
pebbles = my river stones | the stones on the sill
sill = the sill | the window sill
bank = the riverbank | the stream bank
tarn = the tarn | the cold tarn
pork = pork with good crackling | a roast of pork
crackling = the crackling | crackling that snaps
straw = clean straw | new straw on the floor
spitting = this spitting muck | half-rain
ore = ore | good red ore
face = the face | the rock face
pick = my pick | the pick
passroad = the pass road | the road down the valley
lightnight = a long light evening | the summer light, late on
hmph = Hmph | Huh

any
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : #hmph#. I dig all week for #wages# that won't buy a loaf, and the store's never short. #annoyed#.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : The Houses own the hill and I've never once seen one of them up it. I'd not know a House lord if one fell down #face#.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : Feed them first, ask them after. That's how I was raised, and I'll not change it for anyone.
opinion @1 city against 1 : Smoke and shoving, and no #bank# you'd put a paw in. You can have it.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : Nobody up here should go to #bed# #hungry#. Not in this #cold#. Give them a bowl and be done.
opinion @1 road mixed 1 [here.season=winter] : #passroad.capitalize# in winter takes more than it gives. I watch it all the same.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#, #address#. Come in out of #wind#. | #greet#. You look #cold#. Sit by the fire.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=miner] : #greet#. Mind #pick#, I swing wide. | #greet#. Talk loud, #address#. #face.capitalize#'s noisy.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. I'm off up to #work#. | Morning, #address#. Frost on the bank already.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Back down from #work# and starving. | #greet#. Shut the door, it's #cold#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Sit. I'll put the kettle on, #address#. | You. #good.capitalize#. I was hoping it'd be you.
line @1 again.open : You again. #good.capitalize#, saves me walking over. | Back so quick. I'd only just set #pebbles# out.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family|housemates] : #greet#. Come here, then. | #greet#. Mind #pebbles#, I've just set them out.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Quick, #boss#'s watching. | #greet#. Shout it, I can't hear for #pick#.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late, isn't it. | #greet#. Bring a lamp next time.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#. Watch the ice.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Mind the road in the dark. | #farewell#. Straight home, mind.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Same to you.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#! Never heard a word of that. | #oath#. When was this?
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. Old news by now. | I'd heard. #hearsay#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Show me and I'll believe it. | Who says so? I'd want to hear it from them, not you.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. That's #very# hard. | Oh, that's #bad#. That's #bad# news.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#! #good.capitalize#. | Now that's #good#. I'll drink to that.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. Sore, but #fine#. | Not bad. #hungry.capitalize#, mostly.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. #face.capitalize# won't dig itself. | Flat out. Ask me after #work#.
line @1 ask.how : And you? You eating right? | How are you keeping, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Here, sit down before you fall down. | That's a weight, #address#. Let me carry some of it.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. You've come through worse. | It'll come right. I'll help it along if it won't.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, I can't. The shift starts early and I'll be dead on my feet. | Not today, #address#. I've given my evening to the river already.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Next time, then. | Fair enough. I'll ask again #later#.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I mean it. | That's #good# of you. I'll not forget it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. You'd do it for me. | Give over. It was nothing.
line @1 apologise : Sorry. I snapped. I'm like that till I've eaten. | That was short of me. #sorry#.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Right. Back to #face#. | Well. That #ore# won't come out on its own.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I'll go and see if there's any #supper# left.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. #farewell#. | Right you are.
line @1 ack : #bc_right# | #hmph#. Right.
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: never swim the tarn alone, and never in spring. | Pick #pebble# and hold it when you're angry. It helps. Some.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : #warn#. Keep off #passroad# after dark. | #bandits.capitalize# about. Walk in twos.
rule @pick_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=miner
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Come on, come on. #oath#. Give it up. | That's #ore#. That's proper #ore#, that is.

rule @drizzle_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #spitting.capitalize#. Rain or don't, make your mind up. | #annoyed#. Wet through and it's barely raining.

rule @night_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night self.dislikes=night_noise
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Will you lot shut it? Some of us work at dawn. | #oath#. Who's banging at this hour?

rule @stone_bark
when concept=bark working=no here.season=spring|summer
does aside
cooldown 10h
say There's one. Look at that. Smooth as an egg. | Into the pocket. That's #pebbles# up by one.

scene sill_stones
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes|home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Look at #sill#. Forty-odd stones and not a sharp edge among them. | Got a new one off #bank# yesterday. Grey, with a white band right round it. | My pockets are always full of #pebbles#. I wear holes in every coat.
b : Why stones? | Where do you find them? | Why not a bag?
a : Rock's hard all day up at #face#. These are the soft end of it. | Down where #tarn# runs out. The river's done all the work. | A bag, #address#? I'd only fill that too.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | I'll look next time. | #bc_ha#

scene stone_hunt
when topic=pastimes here.season=spring|summer here.outdoors=clear|overcast
does invite / accept / assess
a : Walk down to #bank# with me. The water's low, the good ones show. | I'm off stone-hunting after #supper#. You can come if you keep up. | There's a bend below the falls where #bank# keeps its best. Come and see.
b : Go on, then. I'll come. | I'll keep up. | Show me, then.
a : #good.capitalize#. Look for the ones that shine wet. | Bring a pocket. You'll want one. | #good.capitalize#. Don't tread on any; they're mine.

scene tarn_swim
when topic=pastimes here.season=summer here.outdoors=clear
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Swam #tarn# this morning. Cold enough to stop your heart, and worth it. | I swim every day the ice is off. Only way to get the dust out. | Went in off the high rock again. Came out blue and laughing.
b : You're mad. | Does it work? | Blue?
a : Mad and clean, #address#. That's more than most up here. | Best wash going. The fur comes out a colour again. | Blue. Then warm. Then I'll go in #tarn# again tomorrow.

scene ore_face
when topic=work self.job=miner self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Red #ore# in the low drift today. Heavy as sin and rich with it. | I've been at the same knob of #face# since dawn. It won't give. | Swung #pick# till my arms went dead. Two carts' worth, maybe.
b : Good find. | Leave it for tomorrow. | That's a good day.
a : #good.capitalize#. #boss.capitalize# might even say so. Won't, but might. | I'll not be beat by a rock. #oath#. | #very.capitalize# good. My arms don't agree.

scene gaffer_wet
when topic=work self.job=miner
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / apologise / accept_apology
a : #boss.capitalize# put me on the wet drift again. Third week running. | They've docked us for a short cart. It wasn't short. I loaded it. | Some fool left the ladder rung loose. I near went down the shaft.
b : Did you say anything? | Can you prove it? | Who was it?
a : Said plenty. Too much. Sorry, I'm still hot about it. | Doesn't matter if I can. Sorry, I'm shouting at you. | Didn't ask. Sorry. I'd have hit them, and I'm not proud of it.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | No harm. | I'd have done the same.

scene pork_roast
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #pork.capitalize# on Restday. I've been thinking about it since Hearthday. | The best bit of a pig is #crackling#. I'll fight you for it. | Smell that? Somebody's got #pork# on. I could weep.
b : That long? | You'd fight me? | Go and knock.
a : Every day of the week. It's what gets me up the hill. | I would. And I'd win. Then I'd give you half. | I would if I knew them. #oath#, I'm #hungry#.

scene straw_down
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Put #straw# down this morning. Smells like a summer field in here. | Nothing like #straw# on the floor after a week of dust. | The straw's gone flat and grey. I'll change it Restday if I'm not too #tired#.
b : It does smell good. | It's homely. | You'd better.
a : #good.capitalize#. Wipe your feet, then. | It's how #home# should smell. Clean and yellow. | I will. Remind me if I don't.

scene drizzle
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #spitting.capitalize# again. Not proper rain. Just enough to soak you slow. | I can't abide this. Rain, or don't rain. Pick one. | Wet fur all the way up the hill and all the way down. #annoyed#.
b : It'll clear. | #bc_it_is# | Dry off by the fire.
a : It'd better. I've no patience for #spitting#. | #hmph#. Sorry. It gets under my skin. | I will, and I'll be grumbling the whole time.

scene light_evening
when topic=season|day here.season=summer here.time=dusk
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #lightnight.capitalize#. I'd sit out till midnight if they let me. | This is the bit of the year I'd keep. Warm stone, light sky. | Summer up here's short. I sit out in #lightnight# while it lasts.
b : Sit, then. | It's a good hour. | Every one?
a : I will. Shove over. | #very.capitalize# good. No shift, no snow. | Every one. Winter and #snow# take the rest.

scene night_noise
when topic=home|smalltalk here.time=dusk|night
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / concede / ack
a : Somebody was singing in the lane till all hours. #oath#, I near went out. | Shutters banging half the night. I was up and down like a bucket. | The lot at the inn were loud last night. Some of us start at dawn.
b : Did you go out? | Wedge them. | They do get loud.
a : Didn't. I lay there and counted #pebbles# instead. Calmed me. | I will. Should have last night. You're right. | They do. I'll not grudge them, much. I'll grudge them a bit.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_good# | #bc_fair_enough#

scene road_watch
when topic=travel|memories here.season=winter self.age>=25
does tell.memory / sympathise / assess
tone grave / tender / even
a : I watch #passroad# every winter. I lost someone to a snow, years back. | Somebody I loved went down that road one winter and never came up it. | When #snow# comes, I stand at the door and look down the valley. Old habit.
b : I'm sorry. | That's a long time to watch. | #sympathy#.
a : Long ago. It doesn't go, though. It just gets quieter. | It is. I'll stop when I stop. | #bc_thank_you#. I don't say it often.

scene snow_shut
when topic=weather here.weather=snow
does tell.worry / reassure / assess / ack
a : #snow.capitalize# coming thick. Anyone still on #passroad# wants to hurry. | #passroad.capitalize#'ll shut by dark if this keeps up. | I hate a snow at dusk. You can't see who's still out.
b : They'll be in by now. | #reassure# | They'll have stopped somewhere.
a : I hope so. I'll look anyway. | It always does. And we always manage. | Somewhere warm, I hope. #oath#, I hope.
b? : #bc_hope_so# | #bc_true# | #bc_i_hope_so#

scene spouse
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.spouse# can talk me down quicker than anyone. One look. | I'd swim #tarn# in winter for #self.spouse#. Don't tell anyone. | I'm short with everyone but #self.spouse#. Can't seem to manage it there.
b : That's a good match. | Not a word. | That's love, that is.
a : The best. I don't say it enough. | #good.capitalize#. I've a temper to keep up. | #hmph#. Maybe it is.

scene friend_calm
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# is the one I'd want beside me if the roof came in. | I'd give #self.friend# the pick of my stones. Any one. | When I'm in a black mood, I think of #self.friend# and it passes.
b : That's a friend, then. | Even the banded one? | That's good to have.
a : That's a friend. #good.capitalize#. | Even that. Well. Nearly. | It is. Rarer than #pebble# up here.

scene sorry_earlier
when topic=smalltalk pair.band=friends|family|housemates
does apologise / accept_apology / assess / ack
a : I was short with you this morning. #sorry#. | Sorry about yesterday. I'd had a day at #face# and I took it out on you. | I bit your head off at breakfast. #sorry#. I've been feeling it since.
b : Forget it. | It's done. | It was a bit much.
a : #good.capitalize#. Here, have a stone. The smooth one. | Thank you. I'll try and keep it down. | It was. I'll do better. Or try.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_good# | #bc_ill_try#

scene stranger_fed
when topic=newcomer|player
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : New face down the lane. I sent a bowl of #grub# over before I'd said a word. | There's a stranger at the inn looking frozen. Somebody feed them. | Somebody's come up the pass with snow to the ears. I'd not turn them out.
b : Kind of you. | Somebody will. | Nobody would.
a : Feed them first. Talk after. That's the right order. | If nobody does, I will. | #good.capitalize#. Not up here.

scene bread_dear
when topic=prices|times
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / insist / ack
a : Bread's up again. I'll not even ask why, I'll only shout. | A week's #wages# and the shelf's half empty already. | They say the carts are dear. The carts were dear last year, and the bread was cheaper.
b : Everything's up. | #bc_i_know# | They always say that.
a : Not my #wages#. Those stay put. #annoyed#. | #insist#: something wants changing, and soon. | They do. And I always believe them less.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_we_will_see# | #bc_they_always_do#

scene gossip_plain
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll not dress it up. | Pit-head says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's all I know. | Somebody told me #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Make of it what you like.
b : Who told you? | Is that all? | Hm.
a : Folk. I'll not name them. Take it or leave it. | All of it. I don't add bits. | That's about what I made of it too.

scene good_times
when topic=times world.times=good|boom
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : Full carts down the pass all week. There's even meat in the pot. | #money.capitalize# in my pocket on a Stoneday. That's not happened in a while. | The store's got #pork# again. I bought two. Don't judge me.
b : About time. | Spend it well. | I'll not judge.
a : #bc_about_time#. Long may it last. | I'll spend it on #pork#. Well spent. | #good.capitalize#. One's for you, if you're quick.

story first_stone [topic=memories|pastimes self.age>=25]
  : My #grandad# took me down to #bank# when I was a #child#. Put a stone in my paw, smooth as an egg.
  : Said the river had been at it since before anyone's #grandad#. Said I'd need about as long.
  ask : Do you know what he meant by it?
  b : That you'd a temper, I'd guess.
  b[old] : Patience. They always meant patience.
  : He meant my temper. Still working on it. I've the stone, though.

story thaw_swim [topic=memories|pastimes self.age>=25]
  : Somebody dared me to swim #tarn# the day the ice broke. I was young and daft.
  : I went in. The cold hit like a door slammed on my chest. I came out with no breath and no sense.
  ask : Would you have gone in?
  b : Not for anything. Did you win the dare?
  b[stage=young] : I would! Was it fun?
  : I won it. I couldn't feel my legs for an hour. I've told every young one since: not in spring.

story hard_winter [topic=memories|weather self.age>=30]
  : There was a winter when the snow came early and stayed, and the pass shut for six weeks.
  : Somebody I loved set out to fetch help down the valley. We never saw them again.
  : I was too young to go along. I've never forgiven myself for being glad of it.
  b : You were only young.
  b[old] : I remember that winter. Bad one.
  : I know. Still. Every winter I look down #passroad#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What is it? Quick, I'm starving. | #greet#, #address#. Come in out of #wind#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. #good.capitalize#. Sit, if you're stopping. | #topic.player#! Here, look at this one. Found it yesterday.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. Some of us dig in the morning. Go on, then, #address#.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : What do you want? Say it and go. I've no patience tonight.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=miner] : I dig #ore#. Up the hill at dawn, back down black. #saying#. | #pick.capitalize# and me, all day at #face#. That's the job.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work, I eat, I go down to #bank#. That's me.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Ask at the inn; they talk more than I do.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I'd tell you if I'd heard. I haven't.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Watch the ice. | #farewell#, #address#. Come back when it's warmer.
graft resident.hub
choice What are all those stones on your sill? -> stones
node stones
say River stones. Off the bank below the tarn. Feel this one. Smooth, isn't it? The river did that. Took it years.
mood pleased
free
choice Why collect them? -> stones_why
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node stones_why
say Because I'm all rough edges, and they're not. I hold one when I'm angry. It helps. Some days. Take one, if you like.
mood warm
choice Thank you. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
